: 137, "dislike_count": 1, "description": "SIGN THE PETITION👇 End the 40 year reign of terror. Restore accountability and legal liability to vaccine manufacturers. www.vacsafety.org/petitionShow more This week on VSRF Live, we welcome back Jessica Rose, PhD, for a timely and deeply unsettling conversation: Manufacturing a Poly-Virus Panic.\nDr. Rose is a computational biologist, immunologist, and biostatistician whose work during the Covid era made her one of the most recognized independent scientific voices challenging official public health narratives. Known for her deep analysis of vaccine injury surveillance systems including VAERS, vaccine safety data, viral surveillance systems, and regulatory failures, she returns to examine the sudden flood of new global virus fears now dominating headlines.\nAs media outlets and international health agencies warn about hantavirus, Ebola, “Disease X,” and an expanding list of rare emerging pathogens, Dr. Rose joins us to break down what these viruses actually are, how they spread, what makes them different from one another—and why the public is once again being thrust into a cycle of escalating pandemic fear narratives.\nWe’ll examine the science behind hantavirus and Ebola, including transmission pathways, fatality concerns, surveillance systems, and the growing role of international health authorities such as the WHO in shaping public messaging and emergency response frameworks. Why are rare viruses suddenly dominating headlines again? How are outbreak narratives constructed, amplified, and sustained? And what lessons should the public have learned from the Covid era before accepting a new round of pandemic emergency campaigns?\nWe’ll also revisit one of the most controversial scientific debates to emerge after Covid: DNA contamination findings in the mRNA Covid vaccines. Dr. Rose co-authored work alongside researchers including Kevin McKernan and Phillip Buckhaults examining residual plasmid DNA and manufacturing concerns in the vaccine products—research that sparked intense international debate over quality control, regulatory oversight, and long-term safety questions.\nAs new virus alerts continue to emerge around the world, this is a conversation about much more than hantavirus or Ebola. It’s about the systems, institutions, incentives, and narratives now shaping the public’s understanding of disease itself.\nJoin us live on Tuesday.\n⏰ Time: 7 pm ET, 4 pm PT\n📺 Rumble, YouTube, and X Show less", "thumbnail": "https://hugh.cdn.rumble.cloud/video/fwe2/a7/s8/1/s/7/o/q/s7oqA.qR4e-small-VSRF-Live-229-Manufacturing..jpg", "display_id": "v781zgq", "fulltitle": "VSRF Live #229 - Manufacturing a Poly-Virus Panic", "duration_string": "2:17:49", "upload_date": "20260522", "release_date": "20260526", "release_year": 2026, "is_live": false, "was_live": true, "epoch": 1794321585, "acodec": "aac", "vcodec": "none", "url": "https://hugh.cdn.rumble.cloud/video/fwe2/a7/s8/2/s/7/o/q/s7oqA.Gaa.rec.aac", "format_id": "audio-192p", "tbr": 191, "filesize": 198453708, "width": 0, "height": 192, "protocol": "https", "ext": "aac", "audio_ext": "aac", "video_ext": "none", "vbr": 0, "abr": 191, "resolution": "audio only", "aspect_ratio": 0.0, "http_headers": {"User-Agent": "Mozilla/5.0 (Windows NT 10.0; Win64; x64) AppleWebKit/537.36 (KHTML, like Gecko) Chrome/148.0.0.0 Safari/537.36", "Accept": "text/html,application/xhtml+xml,application/xml;q=0.9,*/*;q=0.8", "Accept-Language": "en-us,en;q=0.5", "Sec-Fetch-Mode": "navigate"}, "format": "audio-192p - audio only", "_type": "video", "_version": {"version": "2026.11.04.232659", "release_git_head": "412e7f0a4b0588fe884a02b344ac66a06538475b", "repository": "yt-dlp/yt-dlp-nightly-builds"}}